==Video Game Appearances==
*''[[Hot Wheels: Beat That!]]''
*''[[Hot Wheels: Track Attack]]''
*''[[w:c:rocketleague:Rocket League|Rocket League]]'', alongside the [[Twin Mill III]]. For more information, see the Bone Shaker's [[w:c:rocketleague:Bone Shaker|Rocket League Wiki article]].
*''[[w:c:forza:Forza Motorsport 6|Forza Motorsport 6]]'' and ''[[w:c:forza:Forza Horizon 3|Forza Horizon 3]]'', via the ''[[w:c:forza:Forza Motorsport 6/Hot Wheels Car Pack|Hot Wheels Car Pack]]'' and the ''[[w:c:forza:Forza Horizon 3/Hot Wheels Expansion|Hot Wheels Expansion]]'' DLC packs, respectively. For more information, see the Bone Shaker's [[w:c:forza:Hot Wheels Bone Shaker|Forza Motorsport Wiki article]].
**It later reappeared in ''Forza Horizon 4'' as an exclusive festival playlist car and ''Forza Horizon 5'' as a car purchasable in the Autoshow for 150,000 credits.
** Also reappeared in ''Forza Motorsport 7''
*''[[w:c:asphalt:Asphalt 8: Airborne|Asphalt 8: Airborne]]'', introduced in the [[w:c:asphalt:Hot Wheels Update|Hot Wheels Update]]. For more information, see the Bone Shaker's [[w:c:asphalt:Hot Wheels Bone Shaker™|Asphalt Wiki article]].
