== Notes ==

* Official Description from the ''Hot Wheels Ultimate Handbook:''
** "A classic hot rod comes to life — or afterlife — in this stripped-down truck rod. The skull grille and skeleton hands around the headlights make it a menacingly frightening opponent. Perhaps no design embodies the Hot Wheels spirit as much as the Bone Shaker, one of the most popular Hot Wheels ever."
** "The Bone Shaker is such an iconic Hot Wheels vehicle that an entire episode of Hot Wheels Let's Race is devoted to it."
** "This 2019 real-life Bone Shaker has a sleek chromed-out skull grille and a special paint job. It has a V-8 engine, 402 horsepower, and a top speed of 160 mph. The shifter even looks like a human spine!"
** "The Bone Shaker first came to life in 2011."

